    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7be39ffe-cad8-57b5-b92f-7425d9b72f69",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 12 & -2 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{22}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{22}=-6+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot (12)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 12 & -2 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 12 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
